title: Angles & Geometry
subject: Maths
level: KS3/GCSE
emoji: 📏
description: Angle rules, polygons, circle theorems and transformations.
---
Angles on a straight line add up to? :: 180°
Angles around a point add up to? :: 360°
Angles in a triangle add up to? :: 180°
Angles in a quadrilateral add up to? :: 360°
Vertically opposite angles are...? :: Equal.
Alternate angles (Z-angles) on parallel lines are...? :: Equal.
Corresponding angles (F-angles) on parallel lines are...? :: Equal.
Co-interior angles (C/U-angles) add up to? :: 180°
Sum of interior angles of an n-sided polygon? :: (n − 2) × 180°
Each exterior angle of a regular n-sided polygon? :: 360° ÷ n
Sum of exterior angles of any polygon? :: 360°
Interior angle of a regular hexagon? :: 120°
What is an isosceles triangle? :: A triangle with two equal sides and two equal base angles.
What is a rhombus? :: A quadrilateral with four equal sides and opposite parallel sides.
Circle theorem: angle in a semicircle? :: 90°
Circle theorem: angle at the centre? :: Twice the angle at the circumference on the same arc.
Circle theorem: angles in the same segment? :: Equal.
Circle theorem: opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral? :: Add up to 180°.
Circle theorem: tangent and radius? :: Meet at 90°.
What are congruent shapes? :: Shapes that are identical in shape and size.
What is a reflection? :: A transformation that flips a shape in a mirror line.
What do you need to describe a rotation? :: Angle, direction and centre of rotation.
What do you need to describe an enlargement? :: Scale factor and centre of enlargement.
